/Title (This Grant Application Guideline aims to help applicants for funding opportunities by providing a roadmap for identifying, applying for, and successfully securing funding for entrepreneurship initiatives. Its purpose is to equip universities and academics with practical knowledge and strategies for effectively accessing financial resources.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1089 0 R
/Prev 1234 0 R
/Next 1327 0 R
>>
endobj
1327 0 obj
<<
/Title (The guideline offers an overview of available funding opportunities, eligibility criteria, and best practices for preparing competitive grant proposals. Whether the goal is to support student-led or professor-led startups, develop innovative educational programs, or foster industry collaborations, this tool can help navigate the funding application process. The following sections are presented on this document:)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1089 0 R
/Prev 1326 0 R
/Next 1235 0 R
>>
endobj
1328 0 obj
<<
/Title (The European Union offers a wide range of funding opportunities to support entrepreneurship in higher education institutions, aiming to foster innovation, economic growth, and social impact. These funding programs provide financial support for projects that align with EU strategic priorities, such as digitalization, sustainability, and social inclusion.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1236 0 R
/Next 1375 0 R
>>
endobj
